## Type islands (where tsc is proven)

| Island | Config | Command |
|--------|--------|---------|
| Day-loop check | [`tsconfig.check.json`](../../tsconfig.check.json) ← `tsconfig.bun.json` | `bun run type-check` |
| Tools ratchet | [`tools/tsconfig.json`](../../tools/tsconfig.json) globs `*.ts` · `cli/*.ts` · `benchmarks/*.ts` | `bun run type-check:tools` |
| STO workspace | `projects/active/sports-terminal-os/tsconfig.check.json` | `bun run type-check:sto` |
| Types audit | walks `extends` for `"types"` | `bun run check:tsconfig-types` |

Expand check: `bun tools/rank-check-includes.ts`. Expand tools: keep globs green or `bun tools/expand-tools-tsconfig.ts`.

### Types allowlist (TS6+)

| Do | Don't |
|----|-------|
| `"types": ["bun"]` | Omit `types` (loads **nothing**) |
| Prefer `"bun"` over `"bun-types"` | Treat `"bun-types"` as the day-loop allowlist |
| `ignoreDeprecations: "6.0"` when `baseUrl` still needed | Forge `'' as AccountId` |
| Add `"react"` / `"node"` only on surfaces that need them | Paste Bun-init onto DOM Pages base blindly |

## Prefer matrix

| Task | Use | Avoid |
|------|-----|-------|
| File read/write | `Bun.file`, `Bun.write`, `.text()` / `.json()` / `.stream()` | `fs.readFile*`, `fs.writeFile*`, `createReadStream` |
| Exists | `await Bun.file(path).exists()` | `existsSync` |
| Glob | `for await (const p of new Bun.Glob(pat).scan({ cwd }))` | `fast-glob`, `globby`, defaulting to `scanSync` |
| Hash digests | `Bun.CryptoHasher`, `Bun.hash` | `crypto.createHash` |
| Passwords | `Bun.password.hash` / `.verify` | `bcrypt`, `argon2` packages |
| Spawn / shell | `Bun.spawn`, `Bun.spawnSync`, `Bun.$` | `child_process` |
| Which | `Bun.which(cmd)` | hand-rolled PATH walks |
| HTTP server | `Bun.serve` | `express`, `fastify` (harness) |
| Fetch | `fetch` / `lib/docs/fetch-page.ts` | `axios` |
| SQLite | `bun:sqlite` | `better-sqlite3` |
| SQL | `Bun.sql` / `bun:sql` when used | `pg`, `mysql2` as default |
| Redis | `Bun.redis` (alias `RedisClient`) | `ioredis` as default |
| S3 / R2 | `Bun.s3` (alias `S3Client`) · `lib/factory/object-store.ts` | ad-hoc AWS SDK in harness |
| Secrets | `Bun.secrets` when applicable | plaintext env for long-lived secrets |
| Test | `bun:test` | `vitest`, `jest` |
| Image | `Bun.Image` · `lib/image-metadata.ts` | `sharp` |
| WebView | `Bun.WebView` (`await using`) | `puppeteer`, `playwright` |
| Cron | `Bun.cron` · [`docs/harness/cron.md`](../../docs/harness/cron.md) | `node-cron` |
| TOML / YAML | `Bun.TOML`, `Bun.YAML` | `@iarna/toml` |
| Semver | `Bun.semver` | npm `semver` |
| Color / ANSI | `Bun.color`, `Bun.stripANSI`, `Bun.stringWidth` | `chalk`, `string-width`, `strip-ansi` |
| Markdown | `Bun.markdown.html` / `.ansi` / `.render` / `.react` (unstable) | `marked` as default |
| Inspect / tables | `Bun.inspect` / `.table` · `lib/console-depth.ts` | raw `util.inspect`, unscoped `console.log(obj)` |
| Env | `Bun.env` | `process.env` in `lib/` + `scripts/` (`check:bun-env`) |
| Paths | `lib/path-bun.ts` | `path` / `node:path` in `lib/` + `tools/` (`check:path-bun`) |
| Deep equals | `Bun.deepEquals` · `lib/deep-equals.ts` | hand-rolled deep compare |
| Peek / settle | `Bun.peek` · `lib/peek-settle.ts` | busy-wait on promises |
| Time / UUID | `Bun.nanoseconds`, `Bun.sleep`, `Bun.randomUUIDv7` · `lib/time.ts` | weak `Date.now()` evidence IDs |
| Entry guard | `import.meta.main` / `lib/shared/tools/entry-guard.ts` | side effects on import |

### Bun.markdown (unstable — four modes)

Types: `bun-types` `namespace markdown` · [reference](https://bun.com/reference/bun/markdown) · mode SSOT [`tools/bun-markdown-modes.ts`](../../tools/bun-markdown-modes.ts). Pin Bun + `@types/bun` together.

| Goal | Call | Key types |
|------|------|-----------|
| Default HTML | `html(md, Options?)` | `Options` |
| Terminal / CLI | `ansi(md, AnsiTheme?)` | `AnsiTheme` |
| Custom string | `render(md, RenderCallbacks?, Options?)` | callbacks + metas |
| React tree | `react(md, ComponentOverrides?, ReactOptions?)` | overrides + props |

```ts
// CLI docs
const out = Bun.markdown.ansi(readme, {
  colors: Boolean(process.stdout.isTTY) && !Bun.env.NO_COLOR,
  columns: process.stdout.columns ?? 80,
  hyperlinks: true,
});
const w = Bun.stringWidth(out);
const plain = Bun.stripANSI(out);

// HTML with heading ids
Bun.markdown.html("## Hello", { headings: { ids: true } });
```

### Snippets (default shapes)

```ts
// Read / write
const text = await Bun.file(path).text();
const data = await Bun.file(path).json();
await Bun.write(path, body);

// Glob
for await (const rel of new Bun.Glob("**/*.ts").scan({ cwd: dir })) { /* … */ }

// Spawn (prefer discrete stdio over invalid string "inherit" if types complain)
const proc = Bun.spawn(["bun", "run", "script.ts"], {
  cwd,
  stdout: "inherit",
  stderr: "inherit",
  stdin: "inherit",
});
await proc.exited;

// Shell
await Bun.$`bun test ${file}`.cwd(dir);

// Hash
const hex = new Bun.CryptoHasher("sha256").update(bytes).digest("hex");

// Config → hash → TOML snapshot (single-pass)
// bun tools/config-toml-snapshot.ts config.json snapshot.toml [--algo=sha3-256]
```

## Known types lag (1.3.14 vs runtime 1.4)

| API | Pattern in-repo |
|-----|-----------------|
| `Bun.TOML.stringify` | [`lib/toml-stringify.ts`](../../lib/toml-stringify.ts) (`factory/cli`, `config-toml-snapshot`) |
| `Bun.isStandaloneExecutable` | `(Bun as …).isStandaloneExecutable` — `tools/fw-build-info.ts` |
| `Bun.write(..., { append: true })` | `appendFile` from `node:fs/promises` — `tools/pulse-daemon.ts` |

When adding a new lag workaround: comment `// types lag bun-types@1.3.x — <docs url>` and prefer Bun again after types bump.

## Escape hatch (ladder)

1. **Narrow Bun cast** (preferred).
2. **One Node primitive** + why (append / missing overload only).
3. **Never** expand into general Node I/O style in harness paths.
4. Reopen when `@types/bun` ≥ runtime minor.

## Wire, brands, console

- Parse once at the edge — [`docs/WIRE_BOUNDARY.md`](../../docs/WIRE_BOUNDARY.md). No `decodeUnknown*` in interior.
- Domain `*Id`: [`lib/types/branded.ts`](../../lib/types/branded.ts) — `as*` / `try*` / `parse*`. Pre-commit: `branded-id-check --staged --strict`.
- Inspect depth: `inspect` / `logDepth` / `logTable` from [`lib/console-depth.ts`](../../lib/console-depth.ts). Bun ignores Node `util.inspect.defaultOptions.depth`.

## Agent workflow

1. `suggest "<api>"` → add `// @see <url>` (or `annotate --write`).
2. Hit prefer matrix / DX catalog before reaching for npm.
3. Stay in a claimed lane; don't sweep other sessions' dirty files.
4. Prove the island you touched:

```bash
bun run type-check
bun run type-check:tools   # if tools/**
bun run check:tsconfig-types
bun run check:bun-env && bun run check:path-bun
bun run test:changed
bun run check:harness      # or lint:bun-native:changed
```

### Parallel agents — report tables

When reporting multi-agent work, separate **Lane** and **Shortcode**:

| Lane | Shortcode | Outcome |
|------|-----------|---------|
| STO | `e3c9ef06` | … |

Link shortcodes as `[label](full-agent-id)` when citing subagents.

